1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Ever look at your OpenAI billing dashboard and wonder where those dollars actually went?

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,200
If you are managing external APIs, tracking unpredictable costs in real time is incredibly difficult.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,800
That is why we built Greenatomy.

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:19,200
Right here in the backend logs, the platform intercepts requests to calculate a complete operational breakdown

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:24,500
for third-party calls, from Anthropic and OpenAI to Google and Azure.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,200
But raw JSON is just the foundation.

7
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,800
Let us look at the live React dashboard.

8
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:34,800
At the top, clean Live Spend Cards give you an instant snapshot,

9
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,800
while the ranked usage table below offers deep granularity.

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,800
Watch how seamlessly we can toggle grouping,

11
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,200
moving from the overall Provider view straight down to specific feature Labels.

12
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:51,000
Now you can pinpoint exactly what your Financial Analysis or Chatbot features cost in real time.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,800
Let us watch the telemetry engine handle a live load.

14
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,200
I am running a traffic seed script to simulate real-world user spikes.

15
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,200
As data streams in, the dashboard updates instantly.

16
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,800
Over on the Charts view, you can see the platform

17
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:09,800
plotting the real-time cost and energy footprint seamlessly.

18
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,200
By the time you review the main overview, Greenatomy has automatically

19
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:16,800
highlighted efficiency drifts, flagged your most expensive API routes,

20
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:20,200
and mapped out your exact cost concentration.

21
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,800
No more surprise bills, just clear visibility.

22
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:30,000
Check out the repository link below to try it out, and let me know your thoughts in the comments.